<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean 3-yr yields end down for third day.</title>
<headline>S.Korean 3-yr yields end down for third day.</headline>
<text>
<p>Yields on three-year benchmark corporate bonds ended down for the third day but dealers said the fall started to slow and the yield would be boxed into the 11.80-11.90 range on Saturday</p>
<p>and early next week.</p>
<p>* 3-yr corporates closed down at 11.90 pct vs 11.92 pct</p>
<p>* 3-mth CDs closed down at 12.00 pct vs 12.10 pct</p>
<p>* Overnight average call rate at 11.84 pct vs 11.70 pct</p>
</text>
